// Title: HackTool - Dumpert Process Dumper Default File
// Sigma ID: 93d94efc-d7ad-4161-ad7d-1638c4f908d8
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2020-02-04 | Modified: 2023-05-09
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.001
// Description: Detects the creation of the default dump file used by Outflank Dumpert tool. A process dumper,
//   which dumps the lsass process memory
// False positives:
//   - Very unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/outflanknl/Dumpert
//   - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/actors-still-exploiting-sharepoint-vulnerability/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_hktl_dumpert.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "dumpert.dmp"
